---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import SiteNav from '../components/marketing/SiteNav.astro';
import Colophon from '../components/marketing/Colophon.astro';

const link = 'text-secondary underline underline-offset-2';
---
<MarketingLayout
  title="Easy installer - HelixScreen"
  description="A desktop app that installs HelixScreen on your printer without a terminal. Download it for Windows, macOS or Linux."
>
  <SiteNav />
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl leading-tight mb-3">HelixScreen easy installer</h1>
    <p class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-3 max-w-[62ch]">
      A desktop app that installs HelixScreen on your printer for you. It finds the printer on your
      network, checks it, and walks you through anything that needs a hand at the printer, such as
      turning on root access or plugging in a USB stick. It only installs what it is sure fits your
      printer, and stops without changing anything when it isn't.
    </p>
    <p class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-10 max-w-[62ch]">
      The printers it covers are listed in the <a href="/installation/" class={link}>installation guide</a>.
      For anything else, use the command-line install from the same page.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl mb-3">Download</h2>
    <div id="installer-download" class="mb-10" data-repo="prestonbrown/helix-installer">
      <p class="ui text-sm text-ink max-w-[62ch]" data-state="loading">Looking for the latest release...</p>
      <noscript>
        <p class="ui text-sm text-ink max-w-[62ch]">
          This page needs JavaScript to find the latest download. Get it from the
          <a href="https://github.com/prestonbrown/helix-installer/releases" class={link}>releases page</a>.
        </p>
      </noscript>
      <p class="ui text-sm text-ink max-w-[62ch] hidden" data-state="none">
        No release of the easy installer is published yet. Until it is, use the command-line install
        in the <a href="/installation/" class={link}>installation guide</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="ui text-sm text-ink max-w-[62ch] hidden" data-state="error">
        The release list could not be loaded. Reload the page in a minute, or use the command-line
        install in the <a href="/installation/" class={link}>installation guide</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="hidden" data-state="ready">
        <p class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-4 max-w-[62ch]">
          Version <span class="tabular" data-field="version"></span>
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4 hidden" data-field="primary-row">
          <a href="#" class="btn btn-strong" data-field="primary"></a>
        </p>
        <p class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-2 max-w-[62ch]">All downloads for this version:</p>
        <ul class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted max-w-[62ch] list-disc pl-5 space-y-1" data-field="all"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-xl mb-3">The first time you open it</h2>
    <p class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-4 max-w-[62ch]">
      Builds without a code-signing certificate are unsigned, and your computer warns you before it runs one. That is expected.
      The warning is about who published the app, not about anything in it.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-base mb-2">macOS</h3>
    <ol class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-3 max-w-[62ch] list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li>Open the downloaded <span class="font-mono">.dmg</span> and drag HelixScreen Installer into Applications.</li>
      <li>Open the app from Applications. macOS blocks it the first time: click <strong>Done</strong> (not Move to Trash).</li>
      <li>
        Open <strong>System Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security</strong> and scroll to the Security
        section. Click <strong>Open Anyway</strong> next to the app's name, then confirm with your
        password or Touch ID.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-6 max-w-[62ch]">
      On macOS 14 and older you can instead right-click (or Control-click) the app and choose
      <strong>Open</strong>. If macOS says the app "is damaged and can't be opened", run
      <span class="font-mono">xattr -cr "/Applications/HelixScreen Installer.app"</span> in Terminal and open it again.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-base mb-2">Windows</h3>
    <ol class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-6 max-w-[62ch] list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li>Run the downloaded <span class="font-mono">-setup.exe</span> (or the <span class="font-mono">.msi</span>).</li>
      <li>
        If SmartScreen shows "Windows protected your PC", click <strong>More info</strong>, then
        <strong>Run anyway</strong>.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h3 class="text-base mb-2">Linux</h3>
    <ul class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-10 max-w-[62ch] list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li>AppImage: make it executable (<span class="font-mono">chmod +x</span> on the file) and run it. Ubuntu 22.04 and newer also need FUSE 2 (<span class="font-mono">sudo apt install libfuse2</span>).</li>
      <li>Debian and Ubuntu: <span class="font-mono">sudo apt install ./HelixScreen.Installer_*.deb</span></li>
      <li>Fedora: <span class="font-mono">sudo dnf install ./HelixScreen.Installer-*.rpm</span></li>
      <li>openSUSE: <span class="font-mono">sudo zypper install ./HelixScreen.Installer-*.rpm</span></li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl mb-3">Flashing a K-Touch</h2>
    <p class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted max-w-[62ch]">
      The installer can flash a BigTreeTech K-Touch over USB. On Linux your user needs the
      <span class="font-mono">dialout</span> group; on Windows you may need the CH340 driver from WCH;
      macOS needs nothing. The <a href="/1.1/guide/install-esp32/#with-the-easy-installer" class={link}>K-Touch guide</a>
      has the details. You can also <a href="/flash/" class={link}>flash from your browser</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Colophon />

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var root = document.getElementById('installer-download');
      if (!root) return;
      var show = function (state) {
        root.querySelectorAll('[data-state]').forEach(function (el) {
          el.classList.toggle('hidden', el.getAttribute('data-state') !== state);
        });
      };
      var field = function (name) { return root.querySelector('[data-field="' + name + '"]'); };

      // One entry per OS: how its files are named in a release, best choice first.
      var KINDS = [
        { os: 'mac', label: 'macOS (Apple silicon and Intel)', re: /universal\.dmg$/ },
        { os: 'win', label: 'Windows installer (.exe)', re: /x64-setup\.exe$/ },
        { os: 'win', label: 'Windows installer (.msi)', re: /x64_en-US\.msi$/ },
        { os: 'linux', label: 'Linux AppImage', re: /amd64\.AppImage$/ },
        { os: 'linux', label: 'Debian and Ubuntu (.deb)', re: /amd64\.deb$/ },
        { os: 'linux', label: 'Fedora and openSUSE (.rpm)', re: /\.x86_64\.rpm$/ }
      ];

      var detectOs = function () {
        var p = (navigator.userAgentData && navigator.userAgentData.platform) || navigator.platform || '';
        var ua = navigator.userAgent || '';
        var s = (p + ' ' + ua).toLowerCase();
        if (/android|iphone|ipad|ipod/.test(s)) return null;
        if (s.indexOf('mac') !== -1) return 'mac';
        if (s.indexOf('win') !== -1) return 'win';
        if (s.indexOf('linux') !== -1 || s.indexOf('x11') !== -1) return 'linux';
        return null;
      };

      fetch('https://api.github.com/repos/' + root.getAttribute('data-repo') + '/releases?per_page=10', {
        headers: { Accept: 'application/vnd.github+json' }
      })
        .then(function (r) {
          if (r.status === 404) return null;
          if (!r.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + r.status);
          return r.json();
        })
        .then(function (list) {
          // The newest published release, prereleases included; drafts never show to visitors.
          var rel = (list || []).filter(function (r) { return !r.draft; })[0];
          if (!rel) return show('none');
          var found = [];
          KINDS.forEach(function (k) {
            var a = (rel.assets || []).filter(function (x) { return k.re.test(x.name); })[0];
            if (a) found.push({ kind: k, url: a.browser_download_url, name: a.name });
          });
          if (!found.length) return show('none');
          field('version').textContent = (rel.tag_name || '').replace(/^v/, '');
          var list = field('all');
          found.forEach(function (f) {
            var li = document.createElement('li');
            var a = document.createElement('a');
            a.href = f.url;
            a.textContent = f.kind.label;
            a.className = 'text-secondary underline underline-offset-2';
            li.appendChild(a);
            list.appendChild(li);
          });
          var os = detectOs();
          var mine = found.filter(function (f) { return f.kind.os === os; })[0];
          if (mine) {
            var btn = field('primary');
            btn.href = mine.url;
            btn.textContent = 'Download for ' + { mac: 'macOS', win: 'Windows', linux: 'Linux' }[os];
            field('primary-row').classList.remove('hidden');
          }
          show('ready');
        })
        .catch(function () { show('error'); });
    })();
  </script>
</MarketingLayout>
